# HHMI Checks Nested Repo Workflow

- Treat `extensions/hhmi-checks` as its own git repository. Run git status, diffs, commits, tests, and package scripts from that directory unless the user explicitly asks for top-level `curvenote` work.
- Prefer scoped package checks while editing text-integrity code:
  - `npm run compile --workspace @hhmi/checks-text-integrity`
  - `npm run test --workspace @hhmi/checks-text-integrity`
  - `npm run lint --workspace @hhmi/checks-text-integrity`
  - `npm run lint:format:fix --workspace @hhmi/checks-text-integrity`
  - `npm run lint:format --workspace @hhmi/checks-text-integrity`
- Quote React Router route paths that contain `$`, for example `'packages/checks-text-integrity/src/routes/app.checks-text-integrity.download-pdf.$id/route.tsx'`.
- If root-level `/Users/stevejpurves/dev/curvenote` checks are required, run them separately and report unrelated root changes or warnings instead of folding them into extension work.
- Prefer pure helpers plus focused specs for route/action behavior so nested-package changes can be tested without loading the entire top-level workspace.
